  ],
  "text": "If Earth were an apple, the air you breathe would be thinner than the skin. From down here the sky looks like it just keeps going. But almost everything you have ever called sky sits in the bottom twelve kilometres. Everest, every cloud, every plane you have ever flown in. All inside that band. Go higher and the air just thins out. There is no wall to hit. So in the nineteen fifties, someone simply picked a number and called it the edge. Nothing changes at that line. The air had already given up long before it. So space does not begin anywhere. We just agreed where to stop calling it sky. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
